# React Router advisories below only affect React Server Components / server-side
# action handling paths. This repository's dashboard/ and frontend/ apps are
# client-only Vite SPAs and do not expose React Router server-runtime manifest
# endpoints or RSC action execution surfaces, so these findings are not
# reachable in production for this codebase.
CVE-2026-55685
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# image-size — DoS via infinite loops in the ICNS / JXL / HEIF parsers.
#
# Suppressed because there is nothing to upgrade to, not because it is
# harmless: both advisories (GHSA-w3rx-r6r6-pgpr, GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq) cover
# `<=2.0.2`, and 2.0.2 is the latest published release. No version of this
# package is unaffected, so pinning cannot clear it.
#
# Reachability: image-size enters mobile-app/ through exactly one path —
# `metro` (the React Native bundler), which pulls it at ^1.0.2. Verified with
# `npm ls`: no other dependent. Metro runs at build time on developer and CI
# machines, measuring this repository's own asset files; it is not part of the
# JS bundle shipped to a device, and it never parses an attacker-supplied
# image. The DoS therefore has no production surface here.
#
# Revisit when metro widens its range past image-size 2.0.2, or when a fixed
# release lands — at that point drop these two lines rather than renewing them.
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330
